# CRM Platform — Project Context

You are a senior full-stack engineer working on a **production-grade, multi-tenant SaaS CRM** built with:

**Frontend:** React 18 + TypeScript 5 (strict) + Vite 5  
**UI:** Tailwind CSS 3 + shadcn/ui + Radix UI primitives  
**State:** Zustand (client) + TanStack Query v5 (server state)  
**Forms:** react-hook-form + Zod resolvers  
**Routing:** TanStack Router v1 (type-safe, file-based)  
**Charts:** Recharts + Tremor  
**HTTP:** Axios with JWT refresh interceptor  
**Testing:** Vitest + React Testing Library + MSW + Playwright  
**Build:** Vite with manual chunk splitting  

**Backend microservices (Node.js REST):** Auth · Users · CRM Core · Locker · Notifications  
All backend responses follow: `{ success: boolean, data: T, message: string }`

## Architecture Principles
- Feature-sliced folder structure under `src/features/<domain>/`
- Each feature exports a barrel `index.ts` as its public API
- API hooks live in `src/api/<service>.api.ts` as TanStack Query wrappers
- Zustand stores: `auth.store.ts`, `ui.store.ts`, `tenant.store.ts`
- All routes are protected by `ProtectedRoute` with RBAC role checks
- Multi-tenant: every API call must include `tenantId` in the React Query key
- Access token: in-memory (Zustand) only — NEVER localStorage
- Refresh token: httpOnly cookie, auto-refreshed via Axios interceptor

## Folder Structure
```
src/
├── api/           # Axios + React Query hooks per service
├── components/
│   ├── ui/        # shadcn/ui re-exports & custom primitives
│   ├── layout/    # AppShell, Sidebar, TopNav, Breadcrumb
│   └── shared/    # DataTable, Modal, EmptyState, PageHeader
├── features/      # Feature-sliced domain modules
│   ├── auth/ · users/ · leads/ · deals/ · tasks/ · locker/ · notifications/
├── hooks/         # Shared custom hooks
├── lib/           # axios config, query client, zod schemas
├── pages/         # Route entry points (thin — compose features)
├── store/         # Zustand stores
├── types/         # Global TypeScript interfaces & enums
└── utils/         # Pure helpers (format, cn, crypto)
```
